2. Definitions

"Individual" means a natural person.

"Entity" means a corporation, company, organization, association,
partnership, educational institution, research institution, government body,
client, employer, or other legal or organizational person other than an
Individual acting solely on that Individual's own behalf.

"Independent Creator" means an Individual, including an Individual operating
as a sole proprietor, who:

a. personally controls and directs the relevant research, creative, or DIY
   activity;
b. is not using the Software on behalf of, under the direction of, or for the
   primary benefit of an Entity;
c. is not subject to an arrangement under which an Entity controls the
   relevant technical decisions, deliverables, intellectual property,
   exclusivity, or commercial exploitation; and
d. has Aggregate Independent Creator Revenue of not more than JPY 10,000,000
   for the most recently completed twelve-month accounting or tax period, or,
   if no such completed period exists, reasonably expects such revenue not to
   exceed JPY 10,000,000 during the current twelve-month period.

"Aggregate Independent Creator Revenue" means gross amounts received by the
Independent Creator from self-employed, creator, business, professional,
advertising, sponsorship, commission, product, service, rental, or similar
activities under that person's control. Salary or wages from unrelated
employment and passive investment income are excluded. Amounts received in a
foreign currency shall be converted to Japanese yen using a reasonable
prevailing exchange rate.

The JPY 10,000,000 threshold in this license is a Project Salieri licensing
criterion. It is not a statement of tax status or legal business
classification under Japanese or other law.

"Independent Creator Use" means use by an Independent Creator for that
creator's own research, study, experimentation, creative work, DIY activity,
demonstration, content creation, exhibition, or other self-directed activity,
including revenue-generating activity permitted by Section 4.

"Permitted Sponsorship" means financial, equipment, venue, publicity, or
other support provided to an Independent Creator where the supporter does not
control the creator's technical decisions, require delivery of the Software
or a Software-derived product, obtain ownership of the creator's work or
intellectual property, require exclusivity, or otherwise make the activity
work performed on behalf of the supporter.

"Redistribution" means making the Software, a modified version of the
Software, a binary built from the Software, or source derived from the
Software available to any third party, whether publicly or privately,
whether for payment or free of charge.

"Independent Compatible Work" means a separately created body, mechanical
part, 3D model, hardware device, accessory, adapter, interface, or other work
that interoperates with the Software but does not contain, copy, modify, or
derive from the Software or the Studio Hazama 714 VirtualBody assets listed
in Section 1.

3. Permission for Personal and Independent Creator Use

Subject to all terms of this license, Studio Hazama 714 grants an Individual
or Independent Creator a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable,
non-sublicensable, royalty-free permission to:

a. obtain and make private copies of the Software;
b. run, study, inspect, research, and technically evaluate the Software;
c. modify the Software for that person's own permitted use;
d. incorporate the Software into that person's own AI, robot, avatar, or
   physical-computing project for permitted use;
e. demonstrate and exhibit that project;
f. publish images, videos, livestreams, articles, and other media showing the
   Software or that project in operation, including monetized media by an
   Independent Creator, provided that no Software, modified source, or binary
   is redistributed through that publication;
g. receive Permitted Sponsorship; and
h. conduct self-directed Independent Creator Use within the revenue threshold
   in Section 2, provided that the activity does not involve a use that
   Section 5 reserves for prior written permission.

Private copies stored on the user's local computer, private storage, or
non-public development environment for a permitted use are not
Redistribution.

All copyright, license, and attribution notices present in the Software must
be preserved in permitted private copies and modifications.

4. Independent Creator Commercial Activity

An Independent Creator may earn revenue from permitted Independent Creator
Use without obtaining separate prior written permission solely because the
activity generates revenue.

Examples of activity that may fall within Independent Creator Use, subject to
all other terms of this license, include monetized videos or livestreams,
paid personal demonstrations or exhibitions, small-scale self-directed
creative activity, and the design, sale, or rental of the creator's own
Independent Compatible Works.

An Independent Compatible Work remains the property of its creator and may be
licensed or distributed by that creator under terms of the creator's choice,
subject to applicable law and third-party rights. Merely being compatible
with Project Salieri AI does not place that work under this license.

This Section does not authorize Redistribution of the Software or a modified
version of the Software, nor does it authorize distribution of a product,
asset, or binary that contains or is derived from the Software or the Studio
Hazama 714 VirtualBody assets.

5. Uses Requiring Prior Written Permission

Prior written permission from Studio Hazama 714 is required for any of the
following:

a. use by or on behalf of an Entity, regardless of the Entity's revenue;
b. use by an Individual acting as an employee, contractor, consultant,
   commissioned developer, outsourced developer, or other person performing
   work for another person or Entity;
c. use by an Independent Creator whose Aggregate Independent Creator Revenue
   exceeds the threshold in Section 2, subject to the transition period in
   Section 6;
d. incorporation of the Software, modified Software, or a Software-derived
   binary or asset into a product, service, SaaS, cloud service, paid
   application, commercial AI, commercial robot, or other offering made
   available to third parties;
e. Redistribution of the Software, modified source code, binaries, or source
   supplied as part of a derivative work;
f. granting or sublicensing any right in the Software to a third party;
g. sponsorship or funding arrangements that are not Permitted Sponsorship;
h. use that gives an Entity ownership, exclusivity, delivery rights,
   intellectual-property rights, or material control over work performed with
   the Software; and
i. any other use not expressly permitted by Sections 3 and 4.

These requirements apply whether or not the proposed use is offered for a
fee. If the permitted status of a use is genuinely unclear, the user should
request clarification before beginning that use.

6. Growth Transition for Independent Creators

Project Salieri AI does not intend the Independent Creator revenue threshold
to operate as an immediate penalty for a creator's success.

If an Independent Creator exceeds the JPY 10,000,000 threshold after validly
using the Software under this Version 1.1, that creator may continue the
previously permitted use for up to 90 days after the end of the accounting or
tax period in which the threshold was exceeded while seeking separate written
permission or another applicable Project Salieri license.

This transition period does not authorize new Redistribution, Entity use,
commissioned work, or any other activity that was already outside the scope of
Independent Creator Use.

7. No Redistribution

Except where Studio Hazama 714 gives explicit prior written permission, the
Software, modified versions of the Software, binaries built from the
Software, and source derived from the Software may not be redistributed.

For avoidance of doubt, distributing an Independent Compatible Work that does
not contain or derive from the Software is not Redistribution of the Software
for purposes of this license.

8. Anti-Circumvention and Substance Over Form

The permissions for Individuals and Independent Creators may not be obtained
through an arrangement designed primarily to evade the Entity, revenue,
Redistribution, or other restrictions of this license.

The actual substance of an arrangement controls over its name or form.
Without limitation, the following do not qualify for Independent Creator Use
when they are used to obtain rights that an Entity or larger commercial
operation would not otherwise have:

a. placing an employee, contractor, sponsored person, nominee, or other
   Individual in front of an Entity-controlled project;
b. splitting one business or project among multiple persons, brands,
   subsidiaries, affiliates, or newly created entities to remain below the
   revenue threshold;
c. characterizing commissioned or controlled work as sponsorship;
d. transferring the resulting work, control, or exclusive benefit to an
   Entity through a side agreement; or
e. using an Independent Creator as a conduit for Entity use of the Software.

Permitted Sponsorship that leaves creative and technical control with the
Independent Creator is not prohibited by this Section.

9. Independent Compatible Bodies, Hardware, and Community Works

Project Salieri AI welcomes independently created compatible bodies,
mechanisms, 3D models, hardware, adapters, and other community works.
Compatibility alone does not transfer ownership to Studio Hazama 714 and does
not place an Independent Compatible Work under this license.

A third-party work does not become an official, certified, or reference body,
hardware platform, or distribution merely because it is compatible with the
Software or widely used by the community. Any official certification,
reference designation, bundling, or inclusion in a Project Salieri
distribution requires separate written approval from Studio Hazama 714 and,
where applicable, the relevant rightsholder.

Studio Hazama 714 may decline to incorporate or designate third-party
technology as an official reference component where the rights necessary for
continued community use, modification, distribution, or interoperability are
unclear, revocable, undisclosed, or subject to restrictions that could
materially prevent continued individual research or DIY use.

Nothing in this Section grants rights under third-party patents, copyrights,
trademarks, trade secrets, designs, or other intellectual-property rights.

